## Summary
In response to new US tariffs, Hyundai is expanding its manufacturing footprint in America. The company's CEO has set a production target that no US assembly plant has ever previously achieved.

## Key Points
- New US tariffs have pushed Hyundai to deepen its investment in American-based manufacturing
- Hyundai's CEO announced a production target that would be unprecedented for any US assembly plant
- The move reflects how trade policy is reshaping where global automakers choose to build vehicles


